# {{.Name}} — app runner

Thin runner for `packages/{{.Name}}`. The app code (Go struct + Astro frontend)
lives entirely in the package; this module only serves it.

| cmd             | mode        | resolver / static                     |
| --------------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------- |
| `./cmd/{{.Name}}`     | production | `astro.MakeFSResolver` (embedded dist) + `http.FileServerFS` |
| `./cmd/{{.Name}}-dev` | development | `astro.MakeServerResolver` + reverse proxy to the astro dev server |

## Ports

- App (Go HTTP server): **{{.AppPort}}** — baked in both runners
- Astro dev server: **{{.AstroPort}}** — baked in `packages/{{.Name}}/astro.config.mjs`

## Run

```sh
make install    # once, at repo root — wires go workspace + pnpm + tools
make dev        # astro (background) + air hot reload → http://localhost:{{.AppPort}}
make web        # astro dev server only → http://localhost:{{.AstroPort}}
make stop       # stop the background astro server
```

## Production

```sh
cd ../../packages/{{.Name}}
pnpm build
cd ../../apps/{{.Name}}
go build -o ./tmp/{{.Name}} ./cmd/{{.Name}}
./tmp/{{.Name}}   # → http://localhost:{{.AppPort}}
```

## Dev-mode notes

- Air watches `packages/astro` and `packages/{{.Name}}` (`.go` only) and
  rebuilds the dev runner on Go changes.
- Astro page edits are hot-reloaded by the astro dev server; the runner
  re-fetches pages on every request, so no Go restart is needed for
  frontend-only changes.